From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ItsLucas <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] platform/surface: aggregator: enable POS events on Surface
 Laptop 7

On the Surface Laptop 7 the EC keeps the touchpad powered off after a
posture change (lid closed -> laptop) until the host has taken the POS
(posture) event. Windows' SurfaceHotPlug driver enables POS events at
every boot. Linux never did on this model, so after a lid close that the
host did not see (e.g. closing the lid right after Windows starts shutting
down, a battery brownout, or some cold boots) the touchpad enumerates but
stays silent, produces no data, and its data-ready IRQ never fires. The
state survives Linux reboots AND a full touch-rail (VREG_TP) power cycle;
only booting Windows or an EC drain clears it.

Enabling the events (TC 0x01, CID 0x0b, payload 26 01 26 00 00, the same
bytes Windows sends) makes the EC deliver the pending posture change at
once, and the touchpad resumes within ~10 ms.

Add the POS tablet-switch node to the SL7 group so the tablet-switch
driver enables POS events at probe. The EC reports one posture source,
ID 1, with 2 for lid closed and 3 for laptop; teach the driver that
source and never report tablet mode for it, since an unknown source would
otherwise be treated as tablet mode and libinput would turn off the
internal keyboard and touchpad.

REQUIRES: CONFIG_SURFACE_AGGREGATOR_TABLET_SWITCH=m (set in config.sl7).
Without it, surface_aggregator_tabletsw.c is not compiled and this patch
does nothing.

Verified on this machine (Romulus15, SAM firmware 26.4.139): revived a
touchpad that had been dead across reboots and a VREG_TP power cycle,
built first as a module overlay and now carried in-tree.

Origin: ItsLucas/surface-laptop-7-ubuntu-kernel commit 004e91d1e125ebdc0547673a3414395b2cdb7e61 ("Enable SAM POS events on the Surface Laptop 7")
Upstream-Status: not upstream; no Signed-off-by from the original author; omarchy-dragon-sl7 issue #25

---
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c |  1 +
 drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_tabletsw.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_registry.c
@@ -297,6 +297,7 @@
 	&ssam_node_root,
 	&ssam_node_tmp_perf_profile_with_fan,
 	&ssam_node_fan_speed,
+	&ssam_node_pos_tablet_switch,
 	&ssam_node_hid_sam_keyboard,
 	/* TODO: evaluate thermal sensors devices when we get a driver for that */
 	NULL,
--- a/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_tabletsw.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/surface/surface_aggregator_tabletsw.c
@@ -331,6 +331,7 @@

 enum ssam_pos_source_id {
 	SSAM_POS_SOURCE_COVER = 0x00,
+	SSAM_POS_SOURCE_LID   = 0x01,
 	SSAM_POS_SOURCE_SLS   = 0x03,
 };

@@ -343,6 +344,12 @@
 	SSAM_POS_COVER_BOOK          = 0x06,
 };

+/* Lid of a clamshell laptop (Surface Laptop 7). */
+enum ssam_pos_state_lid {
+	SSAM_POS_LID_CLOSED = 0x02,
+	SSAM_POS_LID_LAPTOP = 0x03,
+};
+
 enum ssam_pos_state_sls {
 	SSAM_POS_SLS_LID_CLOSED = 0x00,
 	SSAM_POS_SLS_LAPTOP     = 0x01,
@@ -382,6 +389,21 @@
 	}
 }

+static const char *ssam_pos_state_name_lid(struct ssam_tablet_sw *sw, u32 state)
+{
+	switch (state) {
+	case SSAM_POS_LID_CLOSED:
+		return "closed";
+
+	case SSAM_POS_LID_LAPTOP:
+		return "laptop";
+
+	default:
+		dev_warn(&sw->sdev->dev, "unknown device posture for lid: %u\n", state);
+		return "<unknown>";
+	}
+}
+
 static const char *ssam_pos_state_name_sls(struct ssam_tablet_sw *sw, u32 state)
 {
 	switch (state) {
@@ -410,6 +432,9 @@
 	case SSAM_POS_SOURCE_COVER:
 		return ssam_pos_state_name_cover(sw, state->state);

+	case SSAM_POS_SOURCE_LID:
+		return ssam_pos_state_name_lid(sw, state->state);
+
 	case SSAM_POS_SOURCE_SLS:
 		return ssam_pos_state_name_sls(sw, state->state);

@@ -464,6 +489,10 @@
 	case SSAM_POS_SOURCE_COVER:
 		return ssam_pos_state_is_tablet_mode_cover(sw, state->state);

+	case SSAM_POS_SOURCE_LID:
+		/* A clamshell lid has no tablet posture. */
+		return false;
+
 	case SSAM_POS_SOURCE_SLS:
 		return ssam_pos_state_is_tablet_mode_sls(sw, state->state);

